From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Forms with the button below, SIM Lock in the list style

Plinius, for the phone's thumb and the look of the other pages:

- Wi-Fi: libnma's dialogs (connect to a hidden network, create a network,
  802.1X) as form pages: no large icon, no bold caption that repeats the
  page's title, only the explaining sentence; "Connect" (or "Create") is a
  pill below the form (CC_PLINIUS_CONFIRM_BELOW, shell/
  cc-plinius-dialog-pages.c), not in the header bar.
- Wi-Fi hotspot: no "Cancel", back (the arrow and the back swipe) cancels;
  "Turn On" is a pill below the form.
- Mobile Network, SIM Lock: one page in the list style instead of a
  settings view and a PIN view. Below the switch the current PIN is asked
  once the switch is turned; with the lock on and left on the PIN can be
  changed (current, new, confirm). "Apply" below the form. The digit
  filter and the length limit go to the rows' GtkText, as insert-text does
  not reach the wrapping editable.
---
